            <!-- How It Works Architecture Box -->
            <div class="retro-card p-4 m-0 flex flex-col gap-3">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xs uppercase text-prompt m-0">How the pager works</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted m-0">
                1. <strong>Only you:</strong> visitors can only message the owner of the site the pager is on. It can't be used to message other members.<br />
                2. <strong>No chat logs on our server:</strong> live messages aren't saved. If you're offline, a message waits in our database for up to 24 hours and is deleted as soon as you receive it.<br />
                3. <strong>Guests and Cyber-Pass:</strong> visitors without an account get a guest name (e.g. <code>@guest_4291</code>). Clicking <strong>Connect Cyber-Pass</strong> lets members chat as their own handle.<br />
                4. <strong>Replies:</strong> answer from NIM in Neogram; if the visitor still has your site open, the reply shows up in their pager with a chime.
              </p>
            </div>

