          <!-- SECTION 9: CYBERSPACE SECURITY & PRIVACY ARCHITECTURE -->
          <section id="docSection-security" class="docs-section-pane {% if activeTopic != 'security' %}hidden{% endif %} flex flex-col gap-4">

            <div class="p-3 bg-window border border-main text-xs flex flex-col gap-2">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-muted text-xxs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">
                <span>SECURITY &amp; PRIVACY</span>
                <span class="pixel-badge pixel-badge--green text-xxs font-bold">AES-256-GCM</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-prompt m-0">How Neogram protects you and your site</h2>
              <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed m-0">
                The short version: <strong>your photos live on your site, Neogram never touches files outside its own folder, and we keep as little on our server as we can.</strong> The details are below; the <a href="/privacy" class="text-mac underline">privacy policy</a> lists exactly what we store.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Security Grid Features -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <div class="p-3 bg-window border border-main text-xs space-y-1.5">
                <div class="font-bold text-prompt flex items-center gap-1.5">
                  <span></span>
                  <span>Photos aren't kept on our server</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed m-0 text-xxs">
                  Images are uploaded to your host and then deleted from our server (kept only until a failed upload succeeds). Chat history lives in your browser; offline messages wait at most 24 hours.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-3 bg-window border border-main text-xs space-y-1.5">
                <div class="font-bold text-mac flex items-center gap-1.5">
                  <span></span>
                  <span>Your other files are safe</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed m-0 text-xxs">
                  Your Neocities homepage (<code>index.html</code>), blog, styling, and custom files are <strong>never overwritten or touched</strong>. All Neogram assets compile strictly inside your designated subfolder (e.g. <code>/neogram/</code>). Deletes outside that folder's <code>uploads/</code> are refused.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-3 bg-window border border-main text-xs space-y-1.5">
                <div class="font-bold text-amber flex items-center gap-1.5">
                  <span></span>
                  <span>Encrypted API keys</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed m-0 text-xxs">
                  Hosting API keys and tokens are encrypted in our database with <strong>AES-256-GCM</strong> (a fresh IV per write). They're never sent back to the browser or written to logs.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-3 bg-window border border-main text-xs space-y-1.5">
                <div class="font-bold text-green flex items-center gap-1.5">
                  <span></span>
                  <span>Sign-in codes</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed m-0 text-xxs">
                  Sign-in uses single-use 6-digit codes, stored only as a hash. A code stops working after <strong>10 minutes or 5 wrong tries</strong>, and requests are rate-limited per IP and per email/phone.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Technical details -->
            <div class="p-3 bg-window border border-main text-xs space-y-3">
              <span class="font-bold text-xs uppercase text-prompt block">TECHNICAL DETAILS:</span>

              <div class="space-y-2 text-xxs leading-relaxed">
                <div class="p-2 bg-black border border-main text-white space-y-1">
                  <div class="text-prompt font-bold">1. Escaping user text &amp; allowing only http(s) links</div>
                  <p class="text-muted m-0">
                    Visitors can post text through your embeds from any site, so all user-written text is HTML-escaped or inserted with <code>textContent</code>, and links must be <code>http://</code> or <code>https://</code> (<code>javascript:</code> and <code>data:</code> URLs are rejected).
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div class="p-2 bg-black border border-main text-white space-y-1">
                  <div class="text-prompt font-bold">2. File paths</div>
                  <p class="text-muted m-0">
                    Folder names may only use letters, numbers, <code>-</code> and <code>_</code>, and remote file paths are checked segment by segment, so <code>../</code> can't escape your folder on our server or on your host.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div class="p-2 bg-black border border-main text-white space-y-1">
                  <div class="text-prompt font-bold">3. Rate limits</div>
                  <p class="text-muted m-0">
                    API routes are rate-limited per IP (with tighter limits on sign-in, comments, guestbooks and the pager), and chat messages are capped at 64 KB.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div class="p-2 bg-black border border-main text-white space-y-1">
                  <div class="text-prompt font-bold">4. Chat</div>
                  <p class="text-muted m-0">
                    NIM messages pass between connected browsers through our server's memory. If the recipient is offline, the message waits in our database for up to 24 hours and is <strong>deleted as soon as it's delivered</strong>. Chat history is stored only on your devices.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-2 border-t border-main flex-wrap">
              <a href="/privacy" class="pixel-btn pixel-btn--blue text-xs font-bold py-1.5 px-3">
                <span>Privacy Policy</span>
              </a>
